  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision on eco-friendly broiler (chicken)to increase income generation for poor households in Phu Dong, Vietnam</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1 Improved beneficiaries&apos; poultry farming capacity, 1.1.1. Installation of the henhouse and breeding tools, 1.1.2. Training on household-scale poultry raising skills (1day 130 people x Twice a year), 1.1.3. Provide chickens (30 per household_130 households x Twice a year), 1.1.4. Vaccination (4 times x Twice a year), 1.1.5. Provide formula feed (Twice a year), 2.1 Improved beneficiaries&apos; income management capacity, 2.1.1. Training on household-scale financial management skills (1 day 130 people x Twice a year), 3.1 Strengthened SH(producer) group network, 3.1.1. Support Minor renovation of the cultural house and Provision of educational equipment, 3.1.2. Establish 13 SH groups / Support group meetings (10 people for 1 group_total 13 groups), 3.1.3. SH group leaders&apos; field trip training (once a year)</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The per capita GDP in the Phu Dong in 2022 was about 2,621 USD, far below the national average of 4,086 USD. As of 2023, 9 out of a total of 1,528 households (0.59%) were classified as poor, 41 households (2.69%) belonged to the next lowest class (the near poor) households, and 150 households (9.82%) had difficulty in living. The main cause of poverty stems from the lack of skills/information and resources. Through this project, the income level before and after the project was improved by 60% for the poor, and a target index was established to lower the ratio of the number of poor households in Phu Dong from 13.1% to 5% based on official government data. To this end, it aims to reduce regional poverty rates and establish a sustainable living base by increasing income generation of poor households, focusing on,  strengthening the capacity of poor households, broiler support and management&#xc218;&#xd61c;&#xc790;&#xc758; &#xc591;&#xacc4; &#xc0dd;&#xc0b0;&#xc131; &#xd5a5;&#xc0c1;</narrative>
  </description>
